name vis-day-1
timeout 200

# THE EYE, BY DAY -- and the two things that decide what it can see: how big the target LOOKS and how
# much contrast is left of it. doc/sensors.md §9.
#
# A visual contact is not a quieter radar contact. It carries no range, no identity, and no team, and
# it comes into being on ONE inequality: the observed angular subtense of the target's largest presented
# dimension against a threshold of 0.2 deg = 12 arcmin [T4, NTSB via the ATSB cockpit-visibility study],
# scaled up wherever contrast is worse than the reference.
#
#   1. ASPECT. `closer` comes head-on and shows its SPAN (9.14 m, the damage layout's frontal extent
#      doubled); `crosser` cuts across the nose and shows most of its LENGTH (14.6 m). Same threshold,
#      same air, same clock -- so the ratio of the two detection ranges IS the ratio of the two
#      presented dimensions, and nothing else. That "a fighter head-on is worth a fraction of the same
#      fighter side-on" is here a consequence of the geometry, not a coefficient.
#
#   2. THE JOHNSON LADDER. One quantity, three rungs [DERIVED, Johnson 1958 N50: detection 1.0,
#      recognition 4.0, identification 6.4]. A contact becomes "mig29"/"f16" -- the target module's own
#      FBModuleRegistry key -- only at 4x the detection threshold, and that is the ONLY thing this
#      channel can ever say about what it sees. It says WHAT. It never says WHO and never says WHOSE.
#
#   3. THE CLOCK IS PART OF THE MEASUREMENT. `time` gives the sun, and the sun is what decides whether
#      an eye works at all. At 11:00Z over the Broye the sun stands at el 65.8 / az 160.5 -- high and
#      BEHIND a northbound aircraft, so the glare term is 0.99 and this run measures the clean case.
#      vis-night.fbm is this file with one line changed, and it sees nothing at all.
#
# WHAT TO READ (the channel publishes NO range, on purpose -- recompute it from the pose columns of the
# two telemetry files, exactly as mig29-irst.fbm does):
#   events.log   `vis CONTACT` / `RECOGNISED` / `IDENTIFIED` / `DROP`, each with the sizeMrad and the
#                contrast the decision was made on
#   telemetry    vis_contacts, vis_best_mrad (the largest contact's subtense), vis_best_state
#                (1 detected / 2 recognised / 3 identified), vis_glare (1.0 = no glare)
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the verdict AND the pass. A measurement rig, not a task -- the
# waypoints exist only to hold three straight lines. Nothing in the tree CONSUMES this block yet
# (doc/sensors.md §9.9), so no trajectory here differs from one flown before the channel existed.

time 2026-06-21T11:00:00Z

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.60000 6.90000 3000 0.0 300          # due north, level, 300 kt -- the OBSERVER
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off                             # every contact in this trace was SEEN, not painted
  set rwr off
  wp 46.95932 6.90000 3000 300

unit closer
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.68983 6.90327 3000 180.0 300        # 10 km ahead, 250 m right, coming straight back: HEAD-ON
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  wp 46.33051 6.90327 3000 300

unit crosser
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.68085 6.82671 3000 90.0 300         # 9 km ahead, 5.6 km left, crossing: SIDE-ON
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  wp 46.68085 7.21378 3000 300

unit trail
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.62695 6.89673 3000 0.0 200          # 3 km ahead, same heading, 100 kt slower: a SLOW OVERTAKE
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  wp 46.95932 6.89673 3000 200
